Fixed. 5/5 pass.

**Bug:** `token.js:7` used `token.exp < nowSeconds`. Token whose `exp` equal current time evaluated valid — slipped through for one full second window.

```js
function isExpired(token, nowSeconds) {
  return token.exp <= nowSeconds;
}
```

Matches doc comment above it: "expired the moment `exp` is reached". `secondsLeft` needed no change — it delegate to `isExpired`, so boundary case now return 0.

Note: my first run `node --test tests/` failed with `Cannot find module ...\tests` — trailing slash made node treat path as module, not my code. `node --test` from root works.
